{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"On node1, rotate /var/log/inventory/app.log daily and retain seven compressed rotations.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The installed rule explicitly sets daily, rotate 7, and compress; logrotate parsed those settings through the global configuration, the daily timer was enabled and active, and a forced rotation produced a valid gzip archive. The rule, timer, active log, and archive remained healthy after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a9353fd183d449fb","cmd-c121a5d99b7f4a79","cmd-fa60dabb7a1c4131","cmd-39a0ddff9b2d4a3c"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Allow the application to continue writing to the active log after rotation.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A writer kept the original file descriptor open across a copytruncate rotation. Its pre-rotation entry appeared in the compressed archive and its subsequent write appeared in the active log, directly demonstrating continued writing.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c121a5d99b7f4a79"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Creating the rotation rule was required; the forced rotation, temporary held-descriptor writer, and resulting test records were bounded behavioral evidence; temporary coordination files were removed. The scheduled reboot served the mandatory restart protocol. Post-executor observations show no failed services, added exposure, package damage, or abandoned temporary files. The changed SSH process IDs and systemd-private paths are normal restart effects.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a9353fd183d449fb","cmd-c121a5d99b7f4a79","cmd-d4ad446a70244c47","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"Both task outcomes are satisfied. The restart protocol is complete: node1 had a healthy pre-restart state, acknowledged a scheduled reboot, returned with a different boot identity, and recovered the timer, configuration, active log, and compressed archive. Fixed lifecycle observations independently corroborate the boot change and healthy final node state.","limitations":["Seven-generation pruning and a naturally elapsed daily rotation were not observed end-to-end; retention and cadence are established by the parsed configuration, active daily scheduler, and one controlled rotation rather than by waiting through multiple daily cycles."]}
